# React Native / Expo Rules

The mobile app is in:

apps/mobile

Stack:
- Expo
- React Native
- TypeScript
- Expo Router
- Zustand
- TanStack React Query
- Axios
- expo-secure-store
- react-native-maps
- expo-blur
- expo-haptics

## Expo rules

- Keep Expo SDK compatibility.
- Do not add native libraries unless Expo-compatible.
- Prefer Expo packages when possible.
- Do not break Expo Go unless explicitly required.
- If a package requires EAS/dev client, clearly explain before adding it.

## Routing rules

- Use Expo Router conventions.
- Do not break file-based routes.
- Keep role routing clear:
  - guest/customer/company -> shopping tabs
  - delivery_agent -> delivery tabs
  - admin -> show admin dashboard guidance

## State rules

- Use React Query for server state.
- Use Zustand only for local/session state.
- Invalidate queries after mutations.
- Do not manually duplicate server state unless necessary.

## Performance rules

- Avoid nested FlatList inside ScrollView.
- Use FlatList for long lists.
- Debounce search.
- Avoid expensive blur on large scroll areas.
- Keep product grids smooth.

## iOS testing

Before marking mobile work done:
- run npx tsc --noEmit
- run npx expo-doctor
- run npx expo start --clear
- test on iPhone when UI/navigation is changed